and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"be17298264309b61\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3406106255194823, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17522890788497475, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7265013, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:06\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3259756504221951, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18121475631742165, \"vector_similarity\": 0.66375107, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-38\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Build Artifact\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:05] Evan**: Path fix unblocked the Windows packaging attempt — I've got a build artifact out the other end now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:06] Bob**: Does it actually run, or just build?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:24] Evan**: Runs. Installed it on a Windows box and it's passing the same sanity checks we run on Linux.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:26] Diana**: Does this mean Windows compatibility is done?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:36] Evan**: The engineering work for the Windows build is complete — packaging works, the binary is sound. Code-signing is a separate item we haven't even started on yet, so I wouldn't call the whole thing closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:45] Alice**: Understood, we'll track signing on its own. Good progress on the build itself.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 38 slack thread window build artifact channel releas date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 09 05 evan path fix unblock the window packag attempt i ve got a build artifact out the other end now 2026 08 12 09 06 bob doe it actual run or just build 2026 08 12 09 24 evan run instal it on a window box and it s pass the same saniti check we run on linux 2026 08 12 09 26 diana doe this mean window compat is done 2026 08 12 09 36 evan the engin work for the window build is complet packag work the binari is sound code sign is a separ item we haven t even start on yet so i wouldn t call the whole thing close 2026 08 12 09 45 alic understood we ll track sign on it own good progress on the build itself\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e7f9688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"id\": \"61bccaf0a0dfface\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32106665415251384, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1357185773607341, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7535455, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e7f9688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 859, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:30\", \"token_count\": 268, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-58\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Upstream Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Diana**: Bad news on the high-DPI rendering fix. The rotation fix Charlie pushed works for simple cases, but it's completely breaking on documents with nested Form XObjects.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:43] Charlie**: Yeah, I looked into it. The underlying rendering library we're using (`pdf-lib-core`) has a known bug in how it handles coordinates for XObjects when a parent transform is applied.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Alice**: Can we patch it?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:56] Charlie**: No.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:35] Charlie**: It's deep in their C++ core. I've opened an issue with the upstream maintainers, but they haven't responded.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:37] Evan**: We can't wait for an upstream fix if we're hitting the release gate. Can we work around it by flattening the PDFs first?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:51] Charlie**: Flattening might work but it'll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layers.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:29] Alice**: @Diana, @Charlie, let's leave high-DPI rendering blocked for now. We need to decide if we can ship with this limitation or if we need a different rendering library entirely.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:32] Diana**: Agreed. It only affects a small subset of complex documents, but we should document it as a known issue.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 58 slack thread high dpi upstream block channel cipherdoc date 2026 09 10 2026 09 1010 41 diana bad news on the high dpi render fix the rotat fix charli push work for simpl case but it s complet break on document with nest form xobject 2026 09 1010 43 charli yeah i look into it the under render librari we re use pdf lib core ha a known bug in how it handl coordin for xobject when a parent transform is appli 2026 09 1010 55 alic can we patch it 2026 09 1010 56 charli no 2026 09 10 11 35 charli it s deep in their c core i ve open an issu with the upstream maintain but they haven t respond 2026 09 10 11 37 evan we can t wait for an upstream fix if we re hit the releas gate can we work around it by flatten the pdfs first 2026 09 10 11 51 charli flatten might work but it ll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layer 2026 09 10 12 29 alic diana charli let s leav high dpi render block for now we need to decid if we can ship with this limit or if we need a differ render librari entir 2026 09 10 12 32 diana agre it onli affect a small subset of complex document but we should document it a a known issu\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9310f048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"id\": \"72425f09d11fcc84\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31764120470894347, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16943554958420498, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6634544, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9310f048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1371, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:29\", \"token_count\": 414, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnable distributed zero-trust node synchronization for multi-site local deployments, requiring an authenticated handshake between nodes. Validation of the handshake under high-latency networks failed with timeouts; the fix depends on the completed encryption work, but the task remains blocked pending resolution.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Authenticated node-replication handshake completes reliably between nodes.\\n\\n- Handshake succeeds under high-latency network conditions, not only nominal latency.\\n\\n- Blocking timeout issue is resolved before multi-site rollout can proceed.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnable distributed zero-trust node synchronization for multi-site local deployments, requiring an authenticated handshake between nodes. Validation of the handshake under high-latency networks failed with timeouts; the fix depends on the completed encryption work, but the task remains blocked pending resolution.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-04**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because multi-site local deployments need distributed zero-trust node synchronization.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-22**: Diana - Handshake Timeout Block (Blocked)\\n\\n - *Blocked after validation showed handshake timeouts on high-latency networks; resolution depends on the encryption work but remains unresolved.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 descript enabl distribut zero trust node synchron for multi site local deploy requir an authent handshak between node valid of the handshak under high latenc network fail with timeout the fix depend on the complet encrypt work but the task remain block pend resolut clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 accept criterion authent node replic handshak complet reliabl between node handshak succeed under high latenc network condit not onli nomin latenc block timeout issu is resolv befor multi site rollout can proceed clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 descript enabl distribut zero trust node synchron for multi site local deploy requir an authent handshak between node valid of the handshak under high latenc network fail with timeout the fix depend on the complet encrypt work but the task remain block pend resolut clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 activ histori 2026 08 04 alic task creat open open the task becaus multi site local deploy need distribut zero trust node synchron 2026 09 22 diana handshak timeout block block block after valid show handshak timeout on high latenc network resolut depend on the encrypt work but remain unresolv\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e993c5728a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"d487d4d51c3b088f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31183955048684314, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15908450069549027, \"vector_similarity\": 0.668268, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e993c5728a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1197, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:05\", \"token_count\": 534, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"7c000945298cb210\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30565330686576553, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14749778409395076, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67468286, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1559, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:36\", \"token_count\": 450, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"2026-09-22 T029 Windows code signing certificate release gate release hold status\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"No—the **Windows release gate is not cleared** as of 2026-09-22.\n\n- **Engineering completion:** Windows path fixes, packaging, and the binary itself are complete. The artifact installed on Windows and passed the Linux-equivalent sanity checks. [SRC-SLACK-38]\n- **Remaining Windows release hold:** the build is unsigned. A valid code-signing certificate must be procured, signing added to the release-build pipeline, and the signed artifact must pass Defender/SmartScreen without warnings. Until then, installations may be warned or blocked, so T029 remains open. [SRC-GDOC-39] [SRC-CU-CIPH-39]\n- **Overall release:** even after Windows signing clears, the release checklist remains held on the separate T005 Docker image slim-down/CVE gate. [SRC-CU-CIPH-21]"}}
